---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { RENEWAL_PRICE_CENTS, formatUSD } from '../config/promos';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Refunds — Sealshot"
  description="Sealshot's refund policy: 30 days, no questions required, and a 14-day free trial so you can decide before paying."
>
  <section class="section wrap prose" aria-labelledby="refunds-title">
    <p class="kicker">Refunds</p>
    <h1 id="refunds-title">30 days, no questions required</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      If Sealshot isn't right for you, email
      <a href="mailto:support@seal-shot.com">support@seal-shot.com</a> within 30
      days of buying and we'll refund it in full.
    </p>

    <h2>Try it before you pay</h2>
    <p>
      Sealshot has a <strong>14-day free trial</strong> with every feature
      unlocked and no account required. Most reasons for a refund are things the
      trial would have shown you first, so we'd rather you used it — and if you
      bought without trying, that's still no obstacle to a refund.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>
      Purchases are handled by <a href="https://polar.sh" rel="nofollow">Polar</a>,
      our merchant of record, so the refund is processed by them and returns to
      the card you paid with. Email us, or reply to your Polar receipt — either
      reaches us. It usually completes within a few business days, depending on
      your bank.
    </p>
    <p>
      You don't have to give a reason. If something specific didn't work we'd
      genuinely like to hear it, because that's how the app gets better — but
      it's never a condition.
    </p>

    <h2>After a refund</h2>
    <p>
      The license is revoked, and Sealshot returns to its unlicensed state.
      <strong>Nothing you captured is deleted or locked.</strong> Your library
      stays on your Mac, readable and exportable — the same as when a trial ends.
    </p>
    <p>
      How that works, since it's reasonable to wonder: revoked license IDs are
      published in a small public list that Sealshot downloads and checks
      <em>on your Mac</em>. Your license ID is never sent anywhere, and there is
      no server that Sealshot asks about you — see the
      <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Renewals</h2>
    <p>
      An <a href="/renew/">update renewal</a> ({formatUSD(RENEWAL_PRICE_CENTS)})
      is covered by the same 30 days. Since renewing only extends how long you
      receive new versions, and your existing version keeps working either way,
      refunding a renewal simply returns your update window to where it was.
    </p>

    <h2>Volume licenses</h2>
    <p>
      Business and volume licenses are quoted and invoiced individually, so their
      terms are agreed in that quote rather than here. Email
      <a href="mailto:licensing@seal-shot.com">licensing@seal-shot.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Anything unclear before you buy? <a href="/support/">Ask us</a> — we'd
      rather answer a question than process a refund.
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
